<ProductPage locale="en" pageTitle="Anonymous email alias" eyebrow="ANONYMOUS EMAIL · EMAIL ALIAS" titleTop="An anonymous email" titleAccent="that stays under control." description="Create a lasting address for shopping, subscriptions and accounts you intend to keep. Messages arrive in the inbox you already use." primary="Create a free alias" secondary="Compare temp mail" note="One free alias · No phone number · Disable anytime" variant="alias" metrics={[["LONG-LIVED", "Active until disabled"], ["FORWARDS", "To your real inbox"], ["ONE PER SITE", "Leak traceability"], ["ONE CLICK", "Disable anytime"]]} features={[{ no: '01', title: 'No expiry countdown', description: 'Use a lasting alias wherever recovery and future notices matter.', points: ['Keeps receiving while active', 'Suitable for accounts you keep', 'Status is always visible'] }, { no: '02', title: 'Mail reaches your usual inbox', description: 'The alias becomes the public address while your existing mailbox remains the destination.', points: ['No second inbox routine', 'No extra mail client', 'Real address stays private'] }, { no: '03', title: 'One site, one traceable route', description: 'A unique alias shows exactly which service exposed it.', points: ['Leak source is obvious', 'Disable only one address', 'Other aliases stay live'] }]} detailTitle="A lasting address without a lasting exposure" detailText="An alias is a controllable layer between a website and your real inbox. It can stay active for years and still be replaced without changing your private address." faq={[["How is an alias different from temp mail?", "An alias remains active and forwards mail; temp mail is a short-lived inbox that expires."], ["Can a sender see my real address?", "The sender interacts with the alias. Forwarding happens behind the service boundary."], ["Can I disable just one alias?", "Yes. Each alias has an independent active state and does not affect the rest."]]} />
